		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}
	.refs .n {
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: #6d6d68;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.refs a {
		display: inline;
	}
	.refs .src {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.2rem;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: #1f6b46;
		word-break: break-all;
	}
</style>

<Layout
	title="Merry Fren: Bitcoin to the People"
	description="A community token that turns trading activity into Bitcoin for holders."
	pubDate={new Date('September 25 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>

<p>
	<strong>Robin Hood had his Merry Men. Robinhood Chain has Merry Fren.</strong>
</p>

<p>
	The original story was simple. Take surplus. Return it as gold to the people.
</p>

<p>
	Merry Fren carries that idea onto a new rail. $FREN is a fixed-supply token on <a href="https://robinhood.com/chain">Robinhood Chain</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Trading activity in $FREN generates fees. Those fees are captured in Bitcoin. Bitcoin is distributed to eligible holders.
</p>

<p>
	This paper states the thesis, the chain, the token, and the mechanism. It is a project paper, not a specification of Bitcoin.
</p>

<p>
	See also <a href="https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf">Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System</a>.
</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>

<p>
	<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merry_Men">The Merry Men</a> were the company around Robin Hood. They moved value back to ordinary people.
</p>

<p>
	Gold was the unit. The method was the band.
</p>

<p>
	<a href="https://robinhood.com/">Robinhood</a> is one of the world’s largest retail brokers. In 2026 it launched <a href="https://robinhood.com/chain">Robinhood Chain</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Robinhood Chain is an Ethereum layer-2. It was built to settle tokenized stocks, commodities, and on-chain markets.
</p>

<p>
	Memecoins arrived on the same chain. Many of them pair with tokenized stocks and gold. Holders can receive those assets through pairing, fees, or distributions.
</p>

<p>
	Merry Fren applies the same pattern to Bitcoin.
</p>

<p>
	The community is the band. $FREN is the token. Bitcoin is the unit returned to holders.
</p>

<p>
	Official home: <a href="https://merryfren.com/">merryfren.com</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Official voice: <a href="https://x.com/MerryFren">@MerryFren</a>.
</p>

<h2>2. The chain</h2>

<p>
	Robinhood Chain lets real-world assets live next to open token markets.
</p>

<p>
	Tokenized equities and commodities trade on the same network as memecoins. Launchpads let anyone create a fixed-supply token into a pool.
</p>

<p>
	That mix created a new trade. A memecoin can sit across from tokenized Nvidia, Apple, gold, or another listed name.
</p>

<p>
	Activity in the meme moves the paired asset. Some designs pay that asset back to holders.
</p>

<p>
	The chain’s live story is: hold a community token, receive a real asset.
</p>

<p>
	Merry Fren does not wrap a stock. It uses the chain’s activity loop and settles the payout in Bitcoin.
</p>

<h2>3. The token</h2>

<p>
	Name: $FREN. Token of the Merry Men on Robinhood Chain.
</p>

<p>
	Network: <a href="https://robinhood.com/chain">Robinhood Chain</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Launchpad: <a href="https://www.ponsfamily.com/">Pons</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Buy: <a href="https://www.ponsfamily.com/launchpad/0xfb7718C78C6B94Ed82f2B568dF2F79383f873DBa">official Pons launch page</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Supply: fixed. 1,000,000,000. No additional issuance.
</p>

<p>
	A fixed cap matters. Rewards cannot be printed as extra $FREN. If the design works, activity buys Bitcoin. Holders receive Bitcoin, not a larger float.
</p>

<p>
	A deflationary buy-and-burn is planned. More token utility is planned. Neither is live until announced on <a href="https://merryfren.com/">merryfren.com</a> and <a href="https://x.com/MerryFren">@MerryFren</a>.
</p>

<p>
	Always verify the official token address before trading. Copy-cat tickers exist on the same chain.
</p>

<h2>4. The mechanism</h2>

<p>Three steps.</p>

<ol>
	<li><strong>Trade.</strong> People buy and sell $FREN. Trading creates fees.</li>
	<li><strong>Capture.</strong> Those fees are captured in Bitcoin.</li>
	<li><strong>Share.</strong> Bitcoin is distributed to eligible holders under the applicable rules.</li>
</ol>

<p>
	Volume is the input. Bitcoin is the output.
</p>

<p>
	Eligibility and timing follow the live distribution mechanism. This paper does not guarantee a rate, a schedule, or a profit.
</p>

<p>
	No staking. No signup. Just hold $FREN.
</p>

<h3>4.1 Why Bitcoin</h3>

<p>
	Satoshi defined Bitcoin as peer-to-peer electronic cash without a trusted mint. Merry Fren does not replace that system.
</p>

<p>
	It uses Bitcoin as the asset returned to holders. That is the modern equivalent of gold in the older story.
</p>

<h2>5. Incentives</h2>

<p>
	Traders create the fee flow. Holders receive the converted Bitcoin if they are eligible.
</p>

<p>
	The community works if the story and the mechanism stay aligned. Activity in $FREN should produce Bitcoin for the people who hold it.
</p>

<p>
	That is the Merry Men function on this chain. Not a sheriff. A band that moves surplus toward holders.
</p>

<h2>6. NFT collection</h2>

<p>
	A small Merry Fren NFT collection is coming for the early frens.
</p>

<p>
	Characters, supply, and utility will be announced.
</p>

<p>
	Updates: <a href="https://x.com/MerryFren">x.com/MerryFren</a>.
</p>

<h2>7. How to participate</h2>

<ol>
	<li>Read the site: <a href="https://merryfren.com/">merryfren.com</a>.</li>
	<li>Confirm the official token on the <a href="https://www.ponsfamily.com/launchpad/0xfb7718C78C6B94Ed82f2B568dF2F79383f873DBa">Pons launch page</a>.</li>
	<li>Use a wallet that supports Robinhood Chain.</li>
	<li>Follow announcements only from <a href="https://x.com/MerryFren">@MerryFren</a>.</li>
</ol>

<h2>8. Conclusion</h2>

<p>
	Robinhood Chain put stocks, gold, and memecoins on one rail.
</p>

<p>
	Merry Fren takes the Merry Men idea and points the payout at Bitcoin.
</p>

<p>
	Fixed supply. Fees to Bitcoin. Bitcoin to eligible holders.
</p>

<p>
	Robin Hood gave gold to the people. Merry Fren gives Bitcoin to the people.
</p>

